Compact ownership is available through `DNSWEAVER_OWNERSHIP_STORAGE=compact` for TXT-capable providers with zone discovery. It stores claims in compressed pages and per-owner manifests, with no volume or database requirement. Legacy TXT storage remains the default for this release. Upgrade every shared-zone writer before opting in. Selecting `legacy` on the new binary verifies restored per-member markers and any required discovery catalog before removing compact claims. Distinct active owners retain each other's compatible claims; incomplete or conflicting state prevents destructive reconciliation. Same-owner replicas and simultaneous writes to provider APIs that replace whole RRsets still require provider-specific coordination. See the ownership storage guide for migration headroom and recovery limits.
